WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.767
-Oh, my gosh!
I am so happy to see you guys.

00:00:03.767 --> 00:00:06.067
I had an unbelievable adventure
last night.

00:00:06.067 --> 00:00:08.334
-What did you do?
-I went out on the town.

00:00:08.334 --> 00:00:12.534
I painted the town r-r-r-ed,
as Doja Cat would say.

00:00:12.534 --> 00:00:15.100
I went out to a -- John Sykes

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:17.067
invited me to the
Rock &amp; Roll Hall of Fame

00:00:17.067 --> 00:00:19.934
pre-show, like, a dinner.

00:00:19.934 --> 00:00:22.434
And Michele Anthony
from Universal

00:00:22.434 --> 00:00:24.467
and Monte Lipman --
they invited me to this dinner.

00:00:24.467 --> 00:00:25.801
No press.

00:00:25.801 --> 00:00:28.701
They used to do these dinners,
I guess, before the --

00:00:28.701 --> 00:00:30.234
And they stopped doing them.
-Yeah.

00:00:30.234 --> 00:00:31.801
-So they did it.
They brought it back last night.

00:00:31.801 --> 00:00:34.167
We went to a place
called Gabriel's

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:36.334
on Upper West Side.

00:00:36.334 --> 00:00:38.767
And you walk in, it was just --
It was all the nominees

00:00:38.767 --> 00:00:40.133
and all these great people.

00:00:40.133 --> 00:00:42.534
I walked in, I saw --
Immediately, I saw

00:00:42.534 --> 00:00:44.067
Patty Smyth and John McEnroe.

00:00:44.067 --> 00:00:47.100
That was cool.
And so I went over.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:49.934
They introduced me to
Bernie Taupin,

00:00:49.934 --> 00:00:53.534
who is Elton John's -- Yeah, he
wrote all Elton John's things.

00:00:53.534 --> 00:00:55.767
So I was talking to him.
He was funny, making jokes.

00:00:55.767 --> 00:00:57.834
Then there was
The Spinners were there.

00:00:57.834 --> 00:01:00.734
And I went up to The Spinners.
What were The Spinners' jams?

00:01:00.734 --> 00:01:02.133
-Oh, man.

00:01:02.133 --> 00:01:07.567
"Then Came You,"
"I'll Be Around."

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:09.000
-Oh, no, the one I like is...

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:13.467
♪ Could it be I'm falling
in love with you, baby? ♪

00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:15.434
♪ Could it be I'm fall-- ♪

00:01:15.434 --> 00:01:16.801
I should get onstage
with The Spinners.

00:01:16.801 --> 00:01:19.901
-You should spin, yeah.
-I should join The Spinners.

00:01:19.901 --> 00:01:21.100
But I went up to them

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:22.133
and hopefully I wasn't
bothering them.

00:01:22.133 --> 00:01:23.300
But I did.
I went up and I said...

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:25.467
♪ Could it be... ♪
I sang it to them.

00:01:25.467 --> 00:01:26.868
But we talked about
doo-wop and stuff.

00:01:26.868 --> 00:01:28.734
And then I started singing
doo-wop with The Spinners.

00:01:28.734 --> 00:01:30.234
-Oh.
-Then I went over.

00:01:30.234 --> 00:01:31.701
Oh, the night gets crazier.

00:01:31.701 --> 00:01:34.133
And I go over and I'm talking
to my friend Michele

00:01:34.133 --> 00:01:35.868
and I feel a little tap
on my shoulder,

00:01:35.868 --> 00:01:37.400
and it's the coolest ever.

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:39.400
Sheryl Crow in the house.
She says hi to me.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:42.067
I go -- I love Sheryl Crow.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:42.067 --> 00:01:44.100
I love her.

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:47.033
She walks me into this room.
Peter Frampton is there.

00:01:47.033 --> 00:01:50.968
I say hi to Peter Frampton.
H.E.R. was there.

00:01:50.968 --> 00:01:53.400
I sat down with Steve Miller,

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:56.234
and we talked
about "SCTV" for an hour.

00:01:56.234 --> 00:01:58.334
And I laughed with Steve Miller
for an hour.

00:01:58.334 --> 00:02:00.167
We talked about
the Schmenge Brothers?

00:02:00.167 --> 00:02:02.267
-Yeah. Cabbage rolls and coffee.

00:02:02.267 --> 00:02:03.300
-Schmenge Brothers.
-Yeah.

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:04.868
-Talking to Steve Miller
about John Candy.

00:02:04.868 --> 00:02:06.667
-Come on.
-I know. It was making me laugh.

00:02:06.667 --> 00:02:10.367
And then DJ Kool Herc was there,

00:02:10.367 --> 00:02:12.567
who was the father --

00:02:12.567 --> 00:02:14.267
-He invented hip-hop.
-He invented hip-hop.

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:15.701
-Invented hip-hop, yeah.

00:02:15.701 --> 00:02:18.767
-Basically had two turntables
and played two of the same song,

00:02:18.767 --> 00:02:21.167
but just elongated the breaks.

00:02:21.167 --> 00:02:22.968
-The break, yeah.
-And, so, anyways, he was there.

00:02:22.968 --> 00:02:24.667
I talked to him.
He was unbelievable.

00:02:24.667 --> 00:02:28.133
And then, on my way out,
I see Andrew Ridgeley.

00:02:28.133 --> 00:02:30.434
-From Wham!?
-From Wham! Yeah.

00:02:30.434 --> 00:02:32.167
And I go, "Yo,
I have to tell you,

00:02:32.167 --> 00:02:34.334
you came off so cool
in that new documentary."

00:02:34.334 --> 00:02:36.634
He was awesome. I got to
tell -- It was unbelievable.

00:02:36.634 --> 00:02:41.601
And then I left
and I couldn't get a cab.

00:02:41.601 --> 00:02:42.734
So I was just kind of
standing around.

00:02:42.734 --> 00:02:44.133
I just started walking.

00:02:44.133 --> 00:02:46.400
Then this cab pulls over and was
like, "What are you doing, man?"

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:50.434
I go -- And it was John McEnroe.
And I go, "I don't have a car."

00:02:50.434 --> 00:02:52.033
And he goes,
"Oh, come to my apartment

00:02:52.033 --> 00:02:53.400
and then call a car
from my place."

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:56.300
So I went to Johnny Mac's
apartment, and we hung out.

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:57.701
And I got a car from there.
It was amazing.

00:02:57.701 --> 00:02:59.234
But for the first time ever,

00:02:59.234 --> 00:03:01.200
this is the Rock &amp; Roll
Hall of Fame,

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:04.033
is being live-streamed
tomorrow night,

00:03:04.033 --> 00:03:06.801
8:00 p.m., on Disney+.

00:03:06.801 --> 00:03:08.467
So this is the first time
they've ever done this.

00:03:08.467 --> 00:03:10.434
You watch it. It's just gonna --
It's gonna go.

00:03:10.434 --> 00:03:12.300
That's a party. Tomorrow night.

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:15.634
But Kate Bush, Missy Elliott,
Willie Nelson,

00:03:15.634 --> 00:03:18.567
Rage Against the Machine,
The Spinners, Sheryl Crow.

00:03:18.567 --> 00:03:21.701
[ Cheers and applause ]
This is all happening.

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:25.133
Unbelievable. That is
tomorrow night, Disney+.

00:03:25.133 --> 00:03:27.067
Fantastic. And thanks
for everyone for inviting me

00:03:27.067 --> 00:03:28.167
to that secret dinner.

00:03:28.167 --> 00:03:29.801
That was cool.
[ Cheers and applause ]

